# What EAS Build does NOT need uploaded.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS FILE REPLACES .gitignore FOR EAS, IT DOES NOT ADD TO IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The moment this file exists, EAS stops reading `.gitignore` entirely. So every
# rule there has to be repeated here — miss `node_modules/` and the upload goes
# from a few hundred megabytes to several gigabytes. Keep the two in step.
#
# Why this exists: the first build uploaded 661 MB and spent 57 seconds
# compressing it, almost all of which was source material the build never opens.

# ---- Everything from .gitignore ----
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.log
.DS_Store

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.last-batch.json
services/recipe-pipeline/.last-batch.json

# ---- Build-only exclusions, on top of .gitignore ----

# The 311 MB of PNG masters written by the recipe pipeline's `generate-images`
# step. The app never reads these: `build-photo-map.mjs` resolves its requires
# against `apps/mobile/assets/dish-photos`, which holds the 26 MB compressed
# WebP set that actually ships. These are kept in the repository because they
# are expensive to regenerate through the image API, but there is no reason to
# send them to a build server.
assets/dish-photos/

# Version control metadata. EAS already has the fingerprint it needs.
.git/

# The pipeline's raw source data. Its output is committed as
# `seed-recipes.generated.ts` inside the mobile app, so the app builds without it.
recipes/

# NOT excluded, despite being useless to the app: `services/`.
#
# The root package.json declares `workspaces: ["apps/*", "packages/*",
# "services/*"]` and EAS installs with `npm ci`, which is strict about the
# lockfile — a workspace present in `package-lock.json` and absent from the
# upload fails the install outright. It is 152 KB. Not worth the outage.

# Server-side code, deployed by the Supabase CLI rather than by EAS.
supabase/

# Prose.
docs/
*.md
